---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Validate, send and print a GraphQL operation: a request file, or --endpoint with --query

Usage: rustman graphql query [OPTIONS] [REQUEST]

Arguments:
  [REQUEST]
          A graphql request file, its id or its name

Options:
      --endpoint <URL>
          The endpoint of an ad-hoc operation (with --query; no workspace needed)

      --query <TEXT>
          The document of an ad-hoc operation (with --endpoint)

      --no-validate
          Send even when the document fails validation

      --json
          Print the result as one JSON object

      --max-events <N>
          Subscriptions stop after N events (default: the request's max_events, else 10)

      --duration <DURATION>
          Subscriptions stop after this long (default: the request's duration, else 30s)

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --var <K=V>
          Set a variable, above every other source (repeatable): --var k=v

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Total timeout per request, replacing settings.timeout_ms: 500ms, 5s, 2m, or a number of milliseconds

  -k, --insecure
          Do not verify TLS certificates (exchanges are flagged insecure)

      --no-history
          Do not record the exchanges in history

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
